senses.gloss:
--one of the political expedients used by ऋषभ;
1: भा. V. 4. १६.
two fold, the real and the unreal; the first to be applied to the साधुस् (good men); by this the righteous are brought [page३-584+ ३९] under control;
2: M. २२२. 1-१०.
there is no use applying it to the un- righteous. One of the four limbs of नीति, the others being bheda, दान (उप्प्रदान-वि। प्।) and दण्ड (दण्ड pa1ta- वि। प्।).
3: Ib. १४८. ६५-77; Vi. V. २२. १७; ३३. ४०.

(I)--a son of कृष्ण and जाम्बवती; reincarna- tion of Guha;
1: भा. I. १०. २९; ११. १७; १४. ३१; III. 1. ३०; X. ६१. ११; M. ४६. २७; ४७. १८; Vi. IV. १५. ३७; V. ३२. 2;
attended Aniruddha's marriage at भोजकट, went with the वृष्णि army to बाण's city and fought with the son of बाण;
2: भा. X. ६१. २६; ६३. 3;
went out to play and saw a huge lizard in a well and reported it to कृष्ण;
3: ६४. 1-4;
took लक्ष्मणा, daughter of Duryodhana in a svayamvara. The Kurus imprisoned him. Afraid of बलराम's prowess, was released by Duryo- dhana and was given dowry. Went to द्वारका after the राजसूय of युधिष्ठिर and defended the city against शाल्व.
4: Ib X ६८. 1-१२, ४३-52; ७५. २९; ७६. १४; ७७. 4. Vi. V. ३५. 4-5.
Went to स्यमन्तपञ्चक for the solar eclipse.
5: भा. X. ८२. 6.
Went with कृष्ण's sacrificial horse. Fought with Pradyumna at Pra- भास.
6: Ib X. ८९. २२ [2]: ९०. ३३; XI. ३०. १६.
Disguised as a pregnant lady by Yadu youths for fun, approached a sage and asked him whether she would deliver a male child. In anger the sage said that she would give birth to a मुसल (iron rod) which would be death to the Yadu kula. Divested of his attire, the मुसल was seen; causing distress to the Yadus. The king ordered that it must be powdered and thrown into the deep. A bit that was left unpowdered was swallowed by a fish which was caught by a fisherman. The latter fixed it at the tip of his arrow. The particles of the मुसल were thrown ashore and grew to be एरक grass.
7: Ib XI. 1. १३-23; Vi. V. ३७. 7-१०.
Adopted by गण्डूष; had five sons, all warriors, through काशी; one of the five वम्शवीरस्;
8: Br. III. ७१. १९१ and २६०; ७२ 1.
married कश्या, daughter of सुपार्श्व, and mother of पञ्चवीरस् and a number of sons, all with divine sparks;
9: M. ४७. २४.
was looked upon with love by the १६००० [page३-587+ २५] women of कृष्ण and hence they were cursed by कृष्ण to be robbed and dishonoured by robbers. They were rid of the curse by observing अनङ्गदान व्रतम् as prescribed by दाल्भ्य, the sage.
१०: Ib ७०. 5-१०, १७-19, ६२.
Got killed in the यादव struggle at Pra- भास.
११: Vi. V. ३७. ४६.

(II)--a son of हिरण्याक्ष;
1: भा. VII. 2. 4 and १८; Br. III. 5. ३०.
a दानव king; taken to पाताल with Bali by वामन;
2: Ib. III. 6. 4 and ११; IV. २९. १२३; ७३. ८१.
guiles of, towards प्रह्लाद at the instance of हिरण्यकशिपु.
3: Vi. I. १५. १५३; १६. 9.

--a sage of the नैमिषा forest;
1: वा. ३०. ३८; ४९. ९७; ५६. 2; ५७. ८८.
versed in the पुराणस्;
2: Br. II. ३५. ६४-6, ६९.
was addressed by सूत;
3: Br. II. १३. ४१-3; १५. 1; १९. ९९; २८. 2; ३०. 5.
a pupil of Roma- हर्षण.
4: वा. ६१. ५६; ६५. 1; ८९. १६; Vi. III. 6. १७.

(I)--an agreement;
1: Br. II. २६. २६: ३५. १६: ३६. १३५: III. ४८. ४१. वा. ५५. २५: ८८. १३८: ९१. १२: ९६. ५९: १००. ५२.
of Sagara with conquered chiefs;
2: Br. III. ४८. ४६.
broken by Devas.
3: Ib. III. ६६. १२-13: ७२. १२६.

--the seven seas; source of the waters;
1: M. 2. ३४. वा. २७. २६: ५६. ५७.
lord of rivers;
2: M. 8. 6.
southern ocean sacred to पितृस्;
3: Ib. २२. ३९.
rise as the moon waxes and go down as the moon wanes as also at moon rising and setting every day; the rise is estimated to be about ११५ inches in height;
4: Ib. १२३. ३२-4.
the residence of the Lord.
5: वा. ९७. २२.

--the city of Yama, south of Meru;
1: भा. V. २१. 7; VI. 3. 3; Br. II. २१: ३१; M. १२४. २२; वा. ५०. ८८.
reached by कृष्ण and बलराम to recover the dead son of सान्दीपनि;
2: Vi. II. 8. 9; भा. X. ४५. ४२-46.
visited by Arjuna to recover the dead child of द्वारका Bra1hman2a.
3: Ib. X. ८९. ४३.

(II)--a part of the five-year yuga;
1: भा. III. ११. १४; V. २२. 7; Vi. II. 8. ७१-2.
a year, the first among years; is Agni; represented by काव्य pitr2s;
2: Br. II. २१. १३१; २४. ५७, १४१; २८. १५; III. 8. १७; ७२. ३०.
of different kinds--दीव्यसम्वत्सर, Dhruvasamvatsara, पितृसम्वत्सर, and सप्तऋषिसम्वत्सर.
3: Ib. II. २८. २१; २९. १०, १६ and १८.

(II)--also Aurva and वडवामुख;
1: Br. II. 7. 9; १२. ३५-6; २२. ४३; २५. ४५, ५५.
the fire that consumes waters; the प्रलय fire;
2: Ib. IV. 1. १५२; 2. ५०. वा. 6. २९; ५४. ५७
son of Manyu- मान् Agni.
3: Ib. २९. ३३.

(II)--the प्रलय at the end of Kaliyuga; first covering by waters, next by tejas, then by आकाश, then by भूतदि, then by महत्, and lastly by अव्यक्त;
1: वा. २१. ११; १०२. 4, २७-31;
the period ending all manvantaras, each continuing for several yugas;
2: वा. १००. ११८;
impossible to be told in detail.
3: वा. ६१. १२६-27.

--eligible for पार्वण s4ra1ddha;
1: Br. III. १५. ३०; M. १६. १२.
best for a gift;
2: Ib ५४. २१.
to be sung in connection with the rituals in digging tanks, wells, etc.
3: Ib ५८. ३७, ४३.

--a Veda imparted to Jaimini,
1: भा. I. 4. २१; IX. ११. 2; २१. २८; X. 7. १४; ५३. १२; XI. २७. ३१; XII. 6. ७६; ११. ४७; १२. ६२. वा. ३१. ३३; ६५. २६. Vi. III. 4. 9 and १३.
who arranged it under व्यास's guidance; present in वारुणि यज्ञ with विश्वावसुस् and Gandharvas;
2: Br. II. ३४. १५; III. 1. २५.
gave birth to a number of elephants;
3: Ib III. 7. ३३४, ३३९.
learnt by the Asuras;
4: Ib IV. १२. १७.
taught by Jai- mini to his son Sumantu and his grandson सुतवान; the latter's son Sukarma composed सहस्र सम्हिता and taught to his pupils हिरण्यनाभ, Kausalya and पौष्पिञ्जि; ५०० pupils of the latter were the northern chanters of the साम; हिरण्यनाभ's disciples the eastern chanters of the साम; one of his pupils, कृत, taught to his disciples २४ branches [page३-585+ ३५] of the सम्हिता;
5: M. ४९. ७६; वा. ९९. १३०. Vi. III. 6. 1-7.
part of विष्णु;
6: Ib V. 1. ३७.
served with other Vedas as a horse of the chariot of त्रिपुरारि.
7: M. ८५. 5; १३३. ३१;

--neighbouring chieftains; their irritation against the king is a case of internal dissension;
1: Br. III. २७. १३, ३९; २८. १२; ३८. २०; ७४. १२४; M. २२३. 8.
they should behave like fire towards refractory सामन्तस्;
2: Ib. २२६. 7.
residence of;
3: Ib. २२७. १६८; २५४. २१.
followed Haihaya in his hunting expedition;
4: Br. IV. १४. १०.
subordinate to the Kauravas.
5: M. २७२. ३७.

--वैष्णव सामस् for भीमद्वादशि;
1: M. ६९. ४४.
sung by Gandharvas;
2: वा. 2. ३१.
Jaimini learnt them from व्यास;
3: Ib 9. ५०; ६०. १५.
those learned in, know the ब्रह्मा.
4: Ib ७९. ९५; १०१. ३४६.
